      "summary": "Cardrona Alpine Resort is open for skiing today, with yesterday's high winds having eased, leaving clear skies and light winds to start the day. There's been no new snowfall in the past 24 hours, holding the natural base at 112 cm; it's currently 2°C with winds around 43 km/h gusting to 74 km/h, with a mainly fine morning expected before cloud and increasing wind bring snow showers early this evening. Spring conditions prevail across the mountain, with some fresh wind-blown pockets remaining from yesterday. Kindy Conveyor, Learner Conveyors, McDougall's Chondola, Whitestar Express, Valley View, Captains Express, T-Bar and Willow's Quad are all open, with only Soho Express on hold and Wells Pipe Platter closed; 8 of 10 lifts and 9 of 10 terrain zones are running. Main Basin and Valley View open from 8:30am, with Captains and the T-Bar from 9am, and Willows and Soho to follow. (Issued: 11:59am, 21 Sep) The access road is chain-free but chains must always be carried, with an active road hazard advisory in place; the morning is expected to be the best window today, with winds likely to affect chairlift operations into the afternoon. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 8 / 10 Runs Open 0 / 38 Percent open 0 %",
