      "summary": "Treble Cone is open for skiing today, officially into the final week of the season, with mainly fine conditions expected as most developing showers get caught on the divide. There's been no new snowfall in the past 24 hours, with the natural base holding at 150 cm at the top of Home Basin; it's currently 2°C with winds around 35 km/h gusting to 63 km/h. A high overnight freezing level meant little overnight freeze, so firm conditions are expected to soften early into classic spring skiing, with a forecast of severe gale northwesterlies that could interrupt lift operations later. Home Basin Express, Saddle Quad and the Beginner Platter are all running, all 3 of 3 lifts open, with 8 of 9 terrain zones open including Home Basin, Powder Bowl, Matukituki Basin, Saddle Basin and Summit Slopes; only Motatapu Chutes is on hold. Saddle Track has just closed, with a chance the whole Saddle area closes later this afternoon as winds build. (Issued: 11:38am, 21 Sep) Backcountry and skinning access are both open; the access road is chain-free but chains must always be carried, with an active road hazard advisory and a free shuttle running from the bottom of the access road. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 3 / 3 Runs Open 0 / 59 Percent open 0 %",
